   "source": [
    "# Pancreatic islet scRNA-seq preprocessing and quality control\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is a cleaned public version of the preprocessing/QC notebook used for the pancreatic-islet scRNA-seq analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "Only the two libraries used for the manuscript comparison are retained:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Ficoll**\n",
    "- **Gradient-free**\n",
    "\n",
    "Internal sample names and unrelated libraries have been removed. All input/output paths are relative so that the notebook can be placed directly in the GitHub repository.\n",
    "\n",
    "The input is expected to be a SeekSoul/SeekGene-style **filtered feature-barcode matrix** for each library."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Imports and paths\n",
    "\n",
    "Place the two filtered feature-barcode matrices in:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "data/\n",
    "├── ficoll/\n",
    "│   └── filtered_feature_bc_matrix/\n",
    "└── gradient_free/\n",
    "    └── filtered_feature_bc_matrix/\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The final QC-filtered AnnData object and a cell-count summary are written to `data/processed/` and `results/`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import scanpy as sc\n",
    "import scrublet as scr\n",
    "\n",
    "from scipy.stats import median_abs_deviation as mad\n",
    "\n",
    "warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\", FutureWarning)\n",
    "warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\", UserWarning)\n",
    "warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\", RuntimeWarning)\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_DIR = Path(\"data\")\n",
    "RESULTS_DIR = Path(\"results\")\n",
    "PROCESSED_DIR = DATA_DIR / \"processed\"\n",
    "\n",
    "RESULTS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "PROCESSED_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "SAMPLE_DIRS = {\n",
    "    \"Ficoll\": DATA_DIR / \"ficoll\" / \"filtered_feature_bc_matrix\",\n",
    "    \"Gradient-free\": DATA_DIR / \"gradient_free\" / \"filtered_feature_bc_matrix\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "OUTPUT_FILE = PROCESSED_DIR / \"pancreatic_islets_qc.h5ad\"\n",
    "QC_SUMMARY_FILE = RESULTS_DIR / \"qc_cell_counts.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "sc.settings.verbosity = 2\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Load the two libraries\n",
    "\n",
    "Raw UMI counts are stored in `adata.layers[\"counts\"]` before any downstream transformation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def load_library(matrix_dir, workflow):\n",
    "    if not matrix_dir.exists():\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
    "            f\"Matrix directory not found: {matrix_dir}\\n\"\n",
    "            \"Check SAMPLE_DIRS at the top of the notebook.\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "    adata = sc.read_10x_mtx(\n",
    "        matrix_dir,\n",
    "        var_names=\"gene_symbols\",\n",
    "        make_unique=True,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    adata.obs[\"workflow\"] = workflow\n",
    "    adata.layers[\"counts\"] = adata.X.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        f\"{workflow}: \"\n",
    "        f\"{adata.n_obs:,} cells, \"\n",
    "        f\"{adata.n_vars:,} genes\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    return adata\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "adatas = {\n",
    "    workflow: load_library(path, workflow)\n",
    "    for workflow, path in SAMPLE_DIRS.items()\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "initial_cell_counts = {\n",
    "    workflow: adata.n_obs\n",
    "    for workflow, adata in adatas.items()\n",
    "}\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Calculate QC metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "The original notebook calculated mitochondrial, ribosomal, hemoglobin-associated, and top-20-gene fractions for each library."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def calculate_qc_metrics(adata):\n",
    "    adata.var[\"mt\"] = adata.var_names.str.contains(r\"^mt-\", regex=True)\n",
    "    adata.var[\"ribo\"] = adata.var_names.str.contains(r\"^Rp[sl]\", regex=True)\n",
    "    adata.var[\"hb\"] = adata.var_names.str.contains(r\"^Hb[^(P)]\", regex=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "    sc.pp.calculate_qc_metrics(\n",
    "        adata,\n",
    "        qc_vars=[\"mt\", \"ribo\", \"hb\"],\n",
    "        percent_top=[20],\n",
    "        log1p=True,\n",
    "        inplace=True,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Remove redundant total-count columns generated for QC gene sets.\n",
    "    remove = [\n",
    "        \"total_counts_mt\",\n",
    "        \"log1p_total_counts_mt\",\n",
    "        \"total_counts_ribo\",\n",
    "        \"log1p_total_counts_ribo\",\n",
    "        \"total_counts_hb\",\n",
    "        \"log1p_total_counts_hb\",\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "\n",
    "    adata.obs = adata.obs[\n",
    "        [column for column in adata.obs.columns if column not in remove]\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "\n",
    "    return adata\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "adatas = {\n",
    "    workflow: calculate_qc_metrics(adata)\n",
    "    for workflow, adata in adatas.items()\n",
    "}\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Inspect QC distributions\n",
    "\n",
    "These plots are intended as a visual QC check before filtering. They do not apply additional thresholds."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 4.5))\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, (workflow, adata) in zip(axes, adatas.items()):\n",
    "    scatter = ax.scatter(\n",
    "        adata.obs[\"log1p_total_counts\"],\n",
    "        adata.obs[\"log1p_n_genes_by_counts\"],\n",
    "        c=adata.obs[\"pct_counts_mt\"],\n",
    "        s=8,\n",
    "        alpha=0.7,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.set_title(workflow)\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"log1p total counts\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"log1p detected genes\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    colorbar = plt.colorbar(scatter, ax=ax)\n",
    "    colorbar.set_label(\"Mitochondrial transcripts (%)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Primary cell-level QC\n",
    "\n",
    "The original QC notebook used a deliberately permissive pancreas-oriented filter:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. remove cells with hemoglobin-associated transcripts ≥20%;\n",
    "2. flag mitochondrial-content outliers using **5 median absolute deviations (MADs)**;\n",
    "3. remove those mitochondrial outliers;\n",
    "4. retain cells with at least **200 detected genes**;\n",
    "5. retain genes detected in at least **3 cells**.\n",
    "\n",
    "No upper cutoff for total counts or detected genes is applied here, because high-RNA pancreatic populations, particularly acinar cells, can have unusually large UMI counts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def is_outlier(adata, metric, nmads=5):\n",
    "    values = adata.obs[metric]\n",
    "    median = np.median(values)\n",
    "    deviation = mad(values)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return (\n",
    "        (values < median - nmads * deviation)\n",
    "        | (values > median + nmads * deviation)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def primary_qc(adata):\n",
    "    adata = adata.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    adata.obs[\"mt_outlier\"] = is_outlier(\n",
    "        adata,\n",
    "        \"pct_counts_mt\",\n",
    "        nmads=5,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    adata = adata[\n",
    "        (adata.obs[\"pct_counts_hb\"] < 20)\n",
    "        & (~adata.obs[\"mt_outlier\"])\n",
    "    ].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    sc.pp.filter_cells(\n",
    "        adata,\n",
    "        min_genes=200,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    sc.pp.filter_genes(\n",
    "        adata,\n",
    "        min_cells=3,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    return adata\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "for workflow, adata in list(adatas.items()):\n",
    "    before = adata.n_obs\n",
    "    adatas[workflow] = primary_qc(adata)\n",
    "    after = adatas[workflow].n_obs\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        f\"{workflow}: \"\n",
    "        f\"{before:,} -> {after:,} cells \"\n",
    "        f\"after primary QC\"\n",
    "    )\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Doublet detection\n",
    "\n",
    "Scrublet is run separately for each library. As in the original notebook, the expected doublet rate is calculated from the number of initially identified cells:\n",
    "\n",
    "`expected_doublet_rate = 7.6 × 10⁻⁶ × initial cell count`\n",
    "\n",
    "The automatically determined Scrublet threshold is used in this cleaned public version. Predicted doublets are removed before the two libraries are combined."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "scrublet_summary = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for workflow, adata in list(adatas.items()):\n",
    "    expected_rate = 7.6e-6 * initial_cell_counts[workflow]\n",
    "\n",
    "    scrub = scr.Scrublet(\n",
    "        adata.X,\n",
    "        expected_doublet_rate=expected_rate,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    doublet_scores, predicted_doublets = scrub.scrub_doublets(\n",
    "        min_counts=2,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    adata.obs[\"scrublet_score\"] = doublet_scores\n",
    "    adata.obs[\"scrublet_db\"] = predicted_doublets\n",
    "\n",
    "    n_before = adata.n_obs\n",
    "    n_doublets = int(predicted_doublets.sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "    adata = adata[~adata.obs[\"scrublet_db\"]].copy()\n",
    "    n_after = adata.n_obs\n",
    "\n",
    "    adatas[workflow] = adata\n",
    "\n",
    "    scrublet_summary.append(\n",
    "        {\n",
    "            \"workflow\": workflow,\n",
    "            \"expected_doublet_rate\": expected_rate,\n",
    "            \"cells_before_doublet_removal\": n_before,\n",
    "            \"predicted_doublets_removed\": n_doublets,\n",
    "            \"cells_after_doublet_removal\": n_after,\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        f\"{workflow}: expected rate={expected_rate:.4f}; \"\n",
    "        f\"removed {n_doublets} predicted doublets; \"\n",
    "        f\"{n_after:,} cells retained\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "scrublet_summary = pd.DataFrame(scrublet_summary)\n",
    "scrublet_summary\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. QC summary\n",
    "\n",
    "This table explicitly records cell numbers at each stage and can be used to document the order of QC operations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "qc_rows = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for workflow, adata in adatas.items():\n",
    "    scrub_row = scrublet_summary.loc[\n",
    "        scrublet_summary[\"workflow\"] == workflow\n",
    "    ].iloc[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "    qc_rows.append(\n",
    "        {\n",
    "            \"workflow\": workflow,\n",
    "            \"initial_identified_cells\": initial_cell_counts[workflow],\n",
    "            \"cells_after_primary_qc\": int(\n",
    "                scrub_row[\"cells_before_doublet_removal\"]\n",
    "            ),\n",
    "            \"predicted_doublets_removed\": int(\n",
    "                scrub_row[\"predicted_doublets_removed\"]\n",
    "            ),\n",
    "            \"cells_after_doublet_removal\": int(\n",
    "                scrub_row[\"cells_after_doublet_removal\"]\n",
    "            ),\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "qc_summary = pd.DataFrame(qc_rows)\n",
    "qc_summary.to_csv(QC_SUMMARY_FILE, index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "qc_summary\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Combine libraries and save\n",
    "\n",
    "Only **Ficoll** and **Gradient-free** are retained in the combined object. The public workflow names are stored in `adata.obs[\"workflow\"]`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "combined = sc.concat(\n",
    "    adatas,\n",
    "    join=\"outer\",\n",
    "    index_unique=\"_\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "combined.write_h5ad(OUTPUT_FILE)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(combined)\n",
    "print(f\"Saved AnnData: {OUTPUT_FILE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Saved QC summary: {QC_SUMMARY_FILE}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Notes for reproducibility\n",
    "\n",
    "- This notebook starts from filtered feature-barcode matrices generated upstream by the primary SeekSoul/SeekGene processing.\n",
    "- Cell-level QC and Scrublet are performed separately for the two libraries.\n",
    "- This notebook stops after primary QC and doublet removal. Normalization, dimensionality reduction, clustering, annotation, and manuscript figure generation should be performed in the subsequent analysis scripts/notebooks."
   ]
  }
